WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.376 --> 00:00:08.213
If you identify
as a person with disability,

00:00:09.297 --> 00:00:11.007
kindly close your eyes,

00:00:12.175 --> 00:00:14.052
and in your head, repeat after me:

00:00:15.262 --> 00:00:17.806
I am a person

00:00:18.848 --> 00:00:20.141
with disability.

00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:25.105
Thank you.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.693
I have bipolar disorder, type two.

00:00:31.278 --> 00:00:33.321
I am brave to say it now,

00:00:33.363 --> 00:00:38.076
but it actually took me almost 20 years
to be clinically diagnosed.

00:00:38.994 --> 00:00:40.245
I had all the symptoms,

00:00:40.287 --> 00:00:42.998
but I did not seek for medical attention.

00:00:43.999 --> 00:00:46.334
Now I'm giving myself a gift.

00:00:48.753 --> 00:00:50.088
If I can be real honest,

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.882
I was in denial, and I was ashamed of it.

00:00:55.218 --> 00:00:57.679
And here's another interesting story.

00:00:58.346 --> 00:01:00.432
My bipolar diagnosis

00:01:00.432 --> 00:01:04.394
was actually prompted
by having a chronic illness.

00:01:05.312 --> 00:01:06.479
I know.

00:01:07.105 --> 00:01:08.815
And in the Philippines,

00:01:08.815 --> 00:01:13.528
having a chronic disease can be a reason
for employment discrimination,

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.572
which I experienced firsthand.

00:01:16.072 --> 00:01:19.117
And since nobody decided to employ me,

00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:20.910
I decided to employ myself,

00:01:20.952 --> 00:01:22.829
and started my company instead,

00:01:22.871 --> 00:01:25.999
to contribute in building
the future of work

00:01:26.041 --> 00:01:27.792
that leaves no one behind.

00:01:28.418 --> 00:01:29.628
Little did I know --

00:01:29.669 --> 00:01:30.879
(Applause)

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.422
that starting this company --

00:01:32.422 --> 00:01:33.590
thank you --

00:01:34.257 --> 00:01:37.761
also triggered my healing journey

00:01:37.761 --> 00:01:42.265
in embracing my reality
as a person living with disability.

00:01:44.184 --> 00:01:49.731
Worldwide, one in seven people
has a disability.

00:01:51.191 --> 00:01:55.570
Disability is a reality
that affects us all.

00:01:56.446 --> 00:01:59.324
It's part of the diversity
of human experience.

00:01:59.658 --> 00:02:01.451
We may be born with it,

00:02:01.493 --> 00:02:04.829
acquire it through an accident or aging,

00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:07.499
or as a result of trauma and abuse.

00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:13.505
Over one billion people
with disability in the world.

00:02:14.589 --> 00:02:18.301
Hundreds of them are unemployed,

00:02:18.343 --> 00:02:21.638
especially in developing countries
like the Philippines.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:26.142
Their economic inactivity and unemployment

00:02:27.519 --> 00:02:31.022
puts them at a greater risk
of insufficient social protection,

00:02:31.064 --> 00:02:33.942
making them more vulnerable
to extreme poverty.

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:36.486
And the impact on our global economy?

00:02:36.486 --> 00:02:40.573
Trillions of US dollars lost in GDP.

00:02:41.157 --> 00:02:42.701
That's before the pandemic.

00:02:44.119 --> 00:02:50.375
Trillions lost because our society
excludes people like me

00:02:50.375 --> 00:02:52.001
[from] simply getting a job.

00:02:53.086 --> 00:02:54.796
And it's not just me.

00:02:54.838 --> 00:02:59.592
Almost everyone in my team
experienced this systemic problem.

00:03:00.844 --> 00:03:03.680
So we built a virtual school

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.684
that equips our students
with the skills and the mindset

00:03:07.684 --> 00:03:10.186
to work as online service providers.

00:03:11.938 --> 00:03:15.316
We have hundreds of graduates
in over 60 cities and provinces

00:03:15.358 --> 00:03:16.985
all over the Philippines,

00:03:16.985 --> 00:03:21.948
earning an average income
that is 60 percent above the minimum wage.

00:03:22.657 --> 00:03:23.825
But we realize

00:03:23.825 --> 00:03:28.163
that for vocational programs
to be truly sustainable and effective,

00:03:28.997 --> 00:03:32.584
technical skills and employment
support are not enough.

00:03:33.543 --> 00:03:36.838
So we invested in having
a resident psychologist

00:03:36.838 --> 00:03:40.425
to help our students process
their past experiences,

00:03:41.426 --> 00:03:43.094
restore human dignity

00:03:43.845 --> 00:03:45.805
and embrace their realities.

00:03:46.556 --> 00:03:48.975
After completing our program,

00:03:49.017 --> 00:03:51.060
92.6 percent

00:03:52.228 --> 00:03:57.066
claim that they have embraced
and they have understood their disability.

00:03:57.984 --> 00:03:59.652
So my advice to organizations

00:03:59.694 --> 00:04:02.405
that are investing
in talents with disability

00:04:02.447 --> 00:04:04.991
is to look internally

00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:10.079
and identify unconscious bias
of our people around those disabilities.

00:04:10.914 --> 00:04:16.044
From there, validate
and address their fears,

00:04:16.085 --> 00:04:20.006
and work with your people
to cocreate a solution --

00:04:20.006 --> 00:04:22.133
an inclusive solution --

00:04:22.175 --> 00:04:23.301
together.

00:04:24.135 --> 00:04:27.722
This is how we can build and sustain

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:32.352
a safe space that nurtures healing

00:04:33.228 --> 00:04:34.521
and disclosure.

00:04:35.146 --> 00:04:40.443
Disclosure is the key to this systemic
and intergenerational problem.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.447
Speaking from my personal experience,

00:04:44.489 --> 00:04:47.242
the journey to embracing a disability

00:04:47.242 --> 00:04:48.409
is painful.

00:04:49.828 --> 00:04:52.247
It's like coming out of the closet

00:04:52.247 --> 00:04:55.834
or sharing a story of sexual assault.

00:04:58.211 --> 00:05:02.257
It forces us to revisit the hidden past

00:05:02.257 --> 00:05:04.384
or confront an uncertain future.

00:05:05.301 --> 00:05:06.845
It is extremely difficult,

00:05:06.886 --> 00:05:10.890
and it requires a strong support system,

00:05:10.932 --> 00:05:14.811
something that you and I
can build together.

00:05:17.355 --> 00:05:18.523
So that ...

00:05:19.357 --> 00:05:24.404
hopefully, less and less people
will ... suffer in silence.

00:05:26.865 --> 00:05:30.326
We need to effectively heal

00:05:30.368 --> 00:05:32.370
to fight inequality.

00:05:33.496 --> 00:05:35.707
The only way for us to build,

00:05:35.748 --> 00:05:39.878
to truly build a world where people
can truly find belonging,

00:05:41.212 --> 00:05:43.756
is to start with healing.

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:48.052
Thank you.

00:05:48.052 --> 00:05:52.265
(Cheers and applause)

